2026-09-06T10:06Z claude note Re-verification of PR #376 caught this ticket's Context quoting a DECISIONS.md sentence that the same PR's second commit had already reworded away -- "to be fixed in the tooltip rather than by moving the icon" exists nowhere in the ledger, and it contradicted Action 1 four lines below. Requoted verbatim from the ledger as it now stands, which leaves the surface to this ticket. Lesson for the next quoting ticket: a quotation and its source are only safe when the quote is exact, so the pair can be checked mechanically; this one was checked by normalizing whitespace and em dashes and asserting substring containment.
2026-09-06T00:00Z claude note Imagine phase (raid, sonnet): PROCEED, no changes. Blocked-by 0691 now closed. Confirmed no separate aria-label exists in bootstrap.js today (the toolbar `label` attribute doubles as visible text and accessible name), so the tooltip/accessible-name/both surface choice is still genuinely open as the ticket states. `Zotero.Libraries.get(libraryID).name` is an established, simple API already used elsewhere in this repo -- no over-engineering risk. Ready to execute as written.
2026-09-06T12:05Z claude note Surface decided: the tooltip, and only the tooltip. The accessible name was the tempting choice because none exists today -- the toolbar `label` attribute doubles as the accessible name and churns with the spinner glyph and the percentage, which is exactly the instability 0686 wants fixed. But this ticket's first exit criterion requires the coverage figure to travel with the scope, and a string carrying a percentage cannot be stable across state transitions: writing it into aria-label would fight 0686 rather than serve it. 0686 also states its own precondition -- verify assistive-technology claims in a real window before implementing -- which nothing here can do. So the accessible name stays 0686's, unclaimed. Second finding, not in the ticket's premise: `host.list` is `SELECT itemID FROM itemAttachments`, unscoped, so the census covers every library. Naming a single library would have replaced one false scope with another, and `Zotero.Libraries.get(libraryID)` has no correct libraryID to take here; describeSDTScope enumerates from `getAll()` instead -- one name, up to three, then a count.
--- body ---
## Context

Ticket 0694 reviewed where the sitter button belongs and, in doing so, gave
the reason the coverage label needs a scope prefix. The button sits in the
items toolbar, whose scope is one library and one collection, while the
number it shows -- how much of the index is built -- is global background
work. The author's ruling keeps the button there. DECISIONS.md, same day:
the scope mismatch "survives it as a wording problem, and which surface
carries the library name -- tooltip, accessible name, or both -- is ticket
0710's to decide, not this entry's." The surface is this ticket's call, and
the ruling deliberately does not make it.

Ticket 0691 replaced the sitter's SDT jargon with plain language and settled
on "Index 43 %". Its vocabulary table pins that unscoped form, its acceptance
criteria never mention a prefix, and PR #369 ships it as written. So the
prefix is nobody's work until it is filed, which is what this ticket does.

The scoped form 0694 names is:

    Library: My Library — Index 43 %

Where it belongs is part of the work, not a given. The toolbar label is a
narrow strip and 0691 chose its wording for that strip; the tooltip and the
accessible name are the surfaces 0694 identified as able to carry the longer
string in either toolbar position. Ticket 0686 wants a stable accessible
name, so whatever this ticket writes into `aria-label` has to satisfy 0686
too rather than fight it.

## Relevant files

- `bench/sdt-sitter/bootstrap.js` -- builds the toolbar label, its tooltip
  and its accessible name. Moves to `plugins/sdt-sitter/` under ticket 0697;
  rebase onto whichever path is current when this ticket runs.
- `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` -- 0691's source-anchored wording tests, one per
  template site. The new assertion joins them.
- `tickets/0691-sitter-plain-language-vocabulary.erg` -- the vocabulary table
  this extends.
- `tickets/0686-*.erg` -- the stable-accessible-name requirement the
  `aria-label` must keep satisfying.

## Actions

1. Decide which surface carries the scope: tooltip, accessible name, or both.
   Say why in the commit message; the toolbar strip itself is 0691's and does
   not have to grow.
2. Name the library from Zotero's own library record, not a hardcoded
   "My Library" -- a group library must read as itself.
3. Extend 0691's vocabulary table with the scoped form, so one table remains
   the whole vocabulary.

## Test

A source-anchored test in `tests/test_sdt_sitter.py` asserting the chosen
surface carries the library name in front of the coverage figure, scoped to
that site's block rather than the whole file, in 0691's style. Run it against
the unfixed tree first: it must fail, and it must fail because the prefix is
absent, not because the block moved.

A test that greps for the literal "My Library" would pass on a hardcoding and
is the wrong test -- assert that the label is built from the library record.

## Verification

- [x] The new test is red before the change and green after. All three
      source-anchored tests were run against the unfixed tree first; the
      tooltip one failed on "the tooltip states no library scope" with the
      block found, so it failed on the absent prefix and not on a moved
      anchor.
- [x] A group library shows its own name, not "My Library". Driven in
      `tests/sdt_sitter_scheduler.mjs` with "Groupe Climat", a name the
      source cannot contain, so a hardcoding could not satisfy it. Two
      control arms were run on the committed tree: hardcoding the name
      fails both the driven assertion and the source-anchored provenance
      test, and dropping the per-record guard lets a lazily-unloaded group
      library throw out of the tooltip.
- [x] `make check` green.

## Invariants

- 0691's toolbar wording stays as ratified unless this ticket rules
  otherwise on the record; this is an addition, not a revision.
- 0686's accessible name stays stable across state transitions.
- Placement does not change: the button stays in the items toolbar.

## Exit criteria

- [x] The coverage figure reaches the user with its library scope attached,
      on a surface named in the commit message. The surface is the tooltip,
      and only the tooltip; the commit message argues why the accessible
      name was rejected.
- [x] The library name comes from Zotero, not from a literal.
      `describeSDTScope` reads `Zotero.Libraries.getAll()` and asks each
      record for its name.
- [x] 0691's vocabulary table records the scoped form, in three rows: one
      library, several, and more than three.
